<title>SWEDEN: S-E-Banken loses 400 mln Skr tax case.</title>
<headline>S-E-Banken loses 400 mln Skr tax case.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish banking group S-E-Banken said on Thursday it lost a court case concerning 400 million crowns of profit sharing taxes for the years 1988, 1989 and 1990 a second time.</p>
<p>&quot;The case regards differing views on how much profit sharing tax we should pay on payments to public wage earners' funds in the eighties,&quot; S-E-Banken spokeswoman Annika Halldin told Reuters.</p>
<p>The bank has made reservations for almost the entire sum for a long time, S-E-Banken said in a statement, adding that it was considering appealing the ruling.</p>
<p>The bank already lost the case in a lower court in 1993, but appealed.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
